Z||000000||turbo86se||06-22-2001||02:16 AM||||<BR>Has anyone tried installing 5.25" component speakers up front in place on the 4x10's? <BR>I think I read somewhere someone doing this, and it turned out real nice. My 86SE speakerless b/c I put the good ones that were in there in my coupe, since I drive it everyday.<BR>TIA!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-22-2001||02:55 AM||||I installed a set of 4" seperates in mine due to my specific set-up. But I did install 5 1/4" in another Fiero. You need to trim 2 slots in the dash and trim the grill cover in the middle. The 5 1/4" we used were Polk Audio's. The woofer you get needs to have a thin gasket on top. Not a thick one. You need to cut a plate out to fit under the exsisting 4X10 hole. This will hold the tweeter on the outside edge and mount the speaker in the middle. The plate goes under the dash and the speaker mounts on top. Slide the plate in from the top and use the exsisting 4X10 screwhole to mount it. (You need to cut the hole for the tweeter and the 5 1/4" woofer magnet first) You slide the one edge in the slot and press it in the other slot. Then screw it down. Only the middle section of the grill cover needs to be trimmed to fit properly. I wish when I did that install I had my camera then. I would have taken pics.<P>Oops re-read your post, Ignore the part about cutting the tweeter holes. That would be if you used seperates.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||06-22-2001||11:19 AM||||Thanks Oreif, I appreciate the help! I've got an extra dash up in the Fiero attic, I'll have to bring it down and take it with me to the audio store. I've even got a nice set of Boston Acustic Pros, but they're 6.5", would they fit if I mounted them on the bottom? Those speakers rock, and I'd love to use them...<BR>Thanks again,||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-22-2001||11:38 AM||||I mounted a set of Keenwood 5 1/4 separates in my Formula. Did a plate from 1/4" plywood. I mounted the plate on the top (like normal speaker) and 5-1/4" speaker on top of plate. I didn't have to trim anything in the dash. I put a small screw to lift the grill just a little to avoid contact. You can hardly notice it. I think it all depends on the speaker magnet size and the gasket thicknes on top like Orief said.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
